1 2026, then fell 4% in Q2 2026. That was the first decline in three years.\n- Voltaris shipments fell 9% in Q2, the steepest drop among large makers.\n- Its share of Caldrian transformer shipments fell from 31% to 27%. Tarnwell and imports gained.\n- Quarterly revenue went C$905M (2025Q3), C$960M (Q4), C$980M (2026Q1), then C$890M (2026Q2). The Q2 figure is about 9% below Q1.\n- The last four quarters sum to about C$3.735B.\n\n**How I get to 2027**\n- Shipments typically trail orders by about two quarters. The Q2 decline therefore likely reflects weak orders from late 2025 or early 2026, so the weakness should carry into the second half of 2026 and into 2027.\n- If the market is flat to down 2–4% in 2027 and Voltaris holds a share of roughly 27%, revenue would be roughly 5–10% below the trailing level.\n- A share of 27% against the earlier 31% is about 13% lower. If that fully carries through, revenue would sit well below the trailing level. Pricing, mix and non-Caldrian sales would soften this, but I haven't checked them.\n- A run-rate of about C$890M a quarter gives roughly C$3.56B for the year. Another 2–4% drop in the market and a further slip in share would take it toward C$3.4B.\n\n**Upside risk:** an industry recovery, or Voltaris winning back share. The data gives no sign of either yet.\n\n**Limits:** I used only two documents and two short series, covering Q2 2026 at most. The orders data and any guidance from Voltaris would sharpen this estimate.","ttft_ms":1778,"type":"result","duration_ms":20915,"uuid":"d0af62eb-5d50-46d1-8318-498632158ca9","ttft_stream_ms":1645,"time_to_request_ms":242,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":14,"system_prompt":18,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":20,"input_attachments":54,"input_hooks":11,"conversation_append":5,"transcript_persist":23,"tool_pool_refresh":3,"init_message":25,"init_frame_send":8,"engine_pickup":10,"loop_entry":8,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":7,"request_announcements":16,"query_se